---
title: "Noir creator"
note: "A character of a 1940s city of rain and secrets for Krea 2: one of thirty roles (private eye, nightclub singer, crooked cop, mob accountant, reporter, heiress, gangster, forger, safecracker, coroner …) with its clothes and what it holds, or a noir outfit instead, for whom it fits; a bloodhound or a canary in a cage now and then. Mostly black and white, with the signature colour as the one accent that keeps its colour. It keeps what the picture cannot show (EXPORT:): the role, what it holds, a mood, a quirk, two skills, a voice, so a reel that casts it from the gallery reads $hero.role and $hero.voice. One seed is one character, from four sides by the grid: the close views show the head, the shoulders and the clothes, the full-length view the gear and the companion too; $backdrop puts it on the streets instead of the studio, $view one side only to try characters faster."
tags: [krea, characters, references, noir]
---
$colour = __characters/creator/colour__
$gender = {woman:4|man:4|nonbinary person}
$fit = {IF $gender is woman: women|{IF $gender is man: men|all}}
$age = {young:2|prime:4|middle-aged:3|old}
$years = {IF $age is young: {21-26}|{IF $age is prime: {27-39}|{IF $age is middle-aged: {40-58}|{59-75}}}}
$origin = __characters/creator/origin__
$build = __characters/creator/build__
$face = __characters/creator/face__
$eyes = __characters/creator/eyes__
$haircolour = {IF $age is old: {silver|white|iron-grey}|__characters/creator/haircolour__}
$hair = __characters/creator/hair[fit=$fit|all, !modern=yes]__
$beard = {IF $gender is man: {__characters/creator/beard__|none:3}|none}
$mark = __characters/creator/mark__
$role = __characters/noir/role[fit=$fit|all]__
$outfit = {$role.wear:3|__characters/creator/outfit[genre=noir, fit=$fit|all]__:2}
$gear = $role.gear
$motif = __characters/creator/motif[genre=noir|all]__
$companion = {__characters/creator/companion[genre=noir]__|none:4}
$presence = __characters/creator/presence__
$backdrop = {studio:3|street}
$person = a $years-year-old $gender of $origin: $build, $face, $eyes, $hair{IF $beard is not none: , $beard|} and $mark; $role in $outfit, their clothes marked by $motif
$who = $person, with $gear{IF $companion is not none: , $companion|}
# What the picture carries beyond its prompt (EXPORT:): a screenplay that casts it reads $hero.who, $hero.role, $hero.voice …
EXPORT:
  who = $who
  age = $years
  $gender
  $role
  gear = $gear
  companion = $companion
  $colour
  mood = __characters/creator/mood__
  quirk = __characters/creator/quirk__
  skills = {2$$__characters/creator/skill[genre=noir|all]__}
  voice = __characters/creator/voice__
# The grid runs every view: one character from four sides. Set $view to one of them to try characters faster.
# The shot comes first and the picture names only what it can show: the close views the head, the shoulders and the clothes; the full-length view the gear too, and the companion in a sentence of its own.
$look = {monochrome:5|colour:2|comic:2|painted}
$view = {portrait|three-quarter|full-length|profile}
$opening = {IF $look is monochrome: A black-and-white film-noir still, high contrast|{IF $look is colour: A Technicolor photograph, as from a 1940s crime film|{IF $look is comic: A pulp comic panel in heavy black ink|A painted pulp-magazine cover}}}
$shot = {IF $view is portrait: a head-and-shoulders portrait|{IF $view is three-quarter: a head-and-shoulders view|{IF $view is full-length: a full-length view of the whole body, from the top of the head to the shoes,|a strict side profile of the head and shoulders}}}
$stand = They stand straight with the arms relaxed, facing the camera, with $gear, and floor and space around them are in frame.
$pose = {IF $view is portrait: They face the camera.|{IF $view is three-quarter: They are turned three-quarters to the left.|{IF $view is full-length: {IF $companion is not none: $stand With them: $companion.|$stand}|The face is seen exactly from the side, turned 90 degrees to the left, the nose pointing at the left edge of the frame and only one eye visible.}}}
$finish = {IF $look is monochrome: Deep shadows and silver highlights, black and white except for the $colour accents.|{IF $look is colour: Saturated period colour and soft studio key light.|{IF $look is comic: Flat spot colour, $colour on black and white.|Gouache with bold shadows and a weathered paper texture.}}}
$opening: $shot of $person, with $presence. $pose Behind them is {IF $backdrop is studio: a seamless mid-grey studio backdrop|__characters/noir/street__}, in soft, even light. $finish
@size 832x1216
@grid $view
